You have the Prime Wardens set up to go, but want to roll the dice on the environment and villain: Do that with no environment and villain set up, and press randomize, and they will be filled out. Want another combo? Remove the environment and villain and press randomize again.You want to randomize two or three heroes in multiplayer. Select any two or three heroes and press randomize, and you will get the same number of heroes randomized.

[/quote]

&nbsp;

Maybe I&#39;m missing something, but how is the first of these different from the second? &nbsp;If I have (all five) Prime Wardens set up, with no villain/environment, and hit &quot;Randomize,&quot; the game will fill in the Villain/Environment.

&nbsp;

But then, it says that if I select a given number of heroes&nbsp; (ex: five), and hit &quot;Randomize,&quot; the game will spit out a different randomized five-hero combo. &nbsp; 

&nbsp;

 Which is it? &nbsp;If I select five heroes and hit &quot;Randomize,&quot; will the game fill in a villain/environment combo, or select a different random five heroes? 

&nbsp;

